  "aiContextParagraph": "Lalit Modi, a prominent former business executive, has officially obtained British citizenship, marking the conclusion of a sixteen-year period since his departure from India. His residency status in the United Kingdom has remained a subject of significant scrutiny, particularly as Indian authorities continue to pursue the return of high-profile individuals characterized as economic fugitives. This pursuit involves legal inquiries and diplomatic efforts aimed at ensuring such persons face the judiciary within India. Recently, Modi drew public attention following the circulation of a video featuring himself and Vijay Mallya, where he referred to them as 'biggest fugitives of India.' The ensuing reaction led to a formal apology from Modi. This update occurs against a backdrop of broader political discourse in India involving the government's stance on financial crime, legal accountability, and the movement of individuals facing judicial investigation abroad.",
